degree hubs (45, 153, 274), i.e. an ignore-time path exists, which is the confounder here. Testing the only candidate relay in the plausible window: the 182 -> 1860 event at ~26732-27031 is 182's ONLY event in [25832,27031] (step_31), so 182 received nothing within 600 before it and cannot be relaying anything from the earlier 1006 burst. Overall the temporal evidence shows a static/aggregate connection and generally busy hubs (step_01) but no chain of interactions with consecutive gaps <= 600 linking 1006 to 1860; residual uncertainty remains for the later 1860 arrivals (32432-34831, 43232-44431), which I could not fully trace, hence confidence ~0.6."}, "raw_final_response": "```json\n{\n  \"task_id\": \"t_636b848d\",\n  \"decision\": \"absent\",\n  \"mechanism\": \"cascade\",\n  \"entities\": [1006, 1860, 45, 230, 925, 182, 153, 958, 1390],\n  \"window\": [18031, 56431],\n  \"confidence\": 0.62,\n  \"evidence\": [\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_02\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_03\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_04\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_09\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_15\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_17\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_16\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_28\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_20\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_21\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_22\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_23\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_31\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_05\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_06\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_01\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_32\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"}\n  ],\n  \"narrative\": \"1006 and 1860 are each low-degree (5 events, 5 partners) in the window (step_02). 1006's outgoing contacts go to 45, 230, 925, 1680 (step_03) and are concentrated in a single early burst: two events in [20732,21031] (to 45 and 230, steps 18-19) plus one in [21332,21631] (steps 09,15,17), with only isolated later events near ~41000 and ~47000-51600. 1860's incoming contacts come from 153, 182, 958, 1390 (step_04) and occur at ~<20431, ~26732-27031, within [32432,34831], and within [43232,44431] (steps 16,28). None of 1860's in-events falls inside the 600-unit horizon after any 1006 out-event: the nearest subsequent arrival is >5000 time units after 1006's burst ends (steps 20-23 show no 153/182/958/1390 -> 1860 event anywhere in [20732,22831]). The 2-hop static neighbourhoods (steps 05,06) do connect the pair only through very high-degree hubs (45, 153, 274), i.e. an ignore-time path exists, which is the confounder here. Testing the only candidate relay in the plausible window: the 182 -> 1860 event at ~26732-27031 is 182's ONLY event in [25832,27031] (step_31), so 182 received nothing within 600 before it and cannot be relaying anything from the earlier 1006 burst. Overall the temporal evidence shows a static/aggregate connection and generally busy hubs (step_01) but no chain of interactions with consecutive gaps <= 600 linking 1006 to 1860; residual uncertainty remains for the later 1860 arrivals (32432-34831, 43232-44431), which I could not fully trace, hence confidence ~0.6.\"\n}\n```", "total_input_tokens": 126284, "total_output_tokens": 14019, "total_tokens": 140303, "total_latency_ms": 201038, "llm_calls": 14, "schema_repairs": 0, "status": "success", "error": ""}